\p{The velocity in \ref{fnip-0005} is assigned at every point of the
plane. \ref{fnip-0011} draws one solution. Along that solution the
voltage rises and then falls, so the first component of the velocity
takes both signs.}

\p{Where does one component of the velocity vanish, and how do the
solutions fill the plane?}

